# 低频词汇 List10
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List10核心词汇

{{fabricate}}{/ˈfæbrɪkeɪt/}{捏造；制造}{The witness fabricated evidence to mislead the investigation.}}
{{facilitate}}{/fəˈsɪlɪteɪt/}{促进；使便利}{The new software facilitates communication across departments.}}
{{faction}}{/ˈfækʃn/}{派系；小集团}{The party split into rival factions over the issue.}}
{{faculty}}{/ˈfækəlti/}{才能；全体教员}{The faculty voted unanimously in favor of the proposal.}}
{{famine}}{/ˈfæmɪn/}{饥荒；严重缺乏}{The famine affected millions of people across the region.}}
{{fancy}}{/ˈfænsi/}{想象；爱好}{I don't fancy our chances of winning this match.}}
{{fascinate}}{/ˈfæsɪneɪt/}{使着迷；强烈吸引}{The history of ancient civilizations fascinates scholars.}}
{{fate}}{/feɪt/}{命运；天数}{The fate of the project depends on funding decisions.}}
{{fatigue}}{/fəˈtiːɡ/}{疲劳；疲惫}{Decision fatigue can lead to poor judgment.}}
{{favo(u)rable}}{/ˈfeɪvərəbl/}{有利的；赞同的}{The weather conditions were favorable for the outdoor event.}}
{{feast}}{/fiːst/}{盛宴；享受}{The festival is a feast of music, food, and culture.}}
{{federation}}{/ˌfedəˈreɪʃn/}{联邦；联盟}{The federation represents over 200 member organizations.}}
{{feeble}}{/ˈfiːbl/}{虚弱的；无力的}{The patient was too feeble to stand on his own.}}
{{fertile}}{/ˈfɜːtaɪl/}{肥沃的；多产的}{The valley has fertile soil ideal for farming.}}
{{fervent}}{/ˈfɜːvənt/}{热情的；热烈的}{She is a fervent advocate for animal rights.}}
{{fibre}}{/ˈfaɪbər/}{纤维；光纤}{A high-fibre diet promotes good digestive health.}}
{{fierce}}{/fɪəs/}{激烈的；凶猛的}{The fierce debate over immigration policy continues.}}
{{finite}}{/ˈfaɪnaɪt/}{有限的；限定的}{Natural resources are finite and must be conserved.}}
{{flap}}{/flæp/}{拍打；慌乱}{The bird flapped its wings and took flight.}}
{{flatter}}{/ˈflætər/}{奉承；使高兴}{She was flattered by the unexpected compliment.}}
{{flee}}{/fliː/}{逃跑；逃离}{Refugees fled the conflict zone in search of safety.}}
{{flexibility}}{/ˌfleksəˈbɪləti/}{灵活性；柔韧性}{Flexibility is essential in a rapidly changing environment.}}
{{flip}}{/flɪp/}{翻转；轻弹}{She flipped through the pages of the magazine quickly.}}
{{flourish}}{/ˈflʌrɪʃ/}{繁荣；兴旺}{Small businesses can flourish with the right support.}}
{{fluctuate}}{/ˈflʌktʃueɪt/}{波动；涨落}{Oil prices fluctuate based on global supply and demand.}}
{{flush}}{/flʌʃ/}{冲洗；脸红}{The toilet has a dual-flush system to save water.}}
{{foam}}{/fəʊm/}{泡沫；起泡沫}{The waves left foam on the sandy beach.}}
{{fog}}{/fɒɡ/}{雾；迷惑}{Dense fog reduced visibility on the highway.}}
{{folklore}}{/ˈfəʊklɔːr/}{民间传说；民俗}{The region's folklore is rich with tales of mythical creatures.}}
{{footstep}}{/ˈfʊtstep/}{脚步；足迹}{She followed in her mother's footsteps and became a teacher.}}
